  "details": "If some string is stored in copy buffer, error printed on Console when contextual is being closed.\nRepro steps:\n1. Open Graph Editor\n2. Open your text editor. Make a string consisting of a multiple of 4 characters. for example \"1234\", \"abcdzzzz\"\n3. Copy it to OS buffer\n4. Back to Graph Editor. Open contextual menu by right mouse click. Cancel it by ESC key.\n5. Then Error `Tried loading unsupported version of compressed data` appears on Console window\n* on step4, it's the same result if you select any menu item to close.\n* There seems to be no harmful side effects.\nVersion: VRCSDK-UDON-2020.06.18.16.59_Closed_Community_Test\n--- Error details:\nTried loading unsupported version of compressed data\nUnityEngine.Debug:LogError(Object)\nVRC.Udon.Editor.ProgramSources.UdonGraphProgram.UI.UdonGraphExtensions:UnZipString(String) (at Assets/Udon/Editor/ProgramSources/UdonGraphProgram/UI/UdonGraphExtensions.cs:53)\nVRC.Udon.Editor.ProgramSources.UdonGraphProgram.UI.GraphView.UdonGraph:CheckCanPaste(String) (at Assets/Udon/Editor/ProgramSources/UdonGraphProgram/UI/GraphView/UdonGraph.cs:95)\nUnityEngine.GUIUtility:ProcessEvent(Int32, IntPtr) (at C:/buildslave/unity/build/Modules/IMGUI/GUIUtility.cs:179)",
